# Trivy Ignore File for goimg-datalayer
# Use this file to suppress false positives or accepted vulnerabilities
# Format: CVE-ID or vulnerability ID (one per line)
# Add comments explaining why each vulnerability is ignored

# =============================================================================
# Development Dependencies - Not Shipped in Production
# =============================================================================

# Note: Add specific CVEs here if they only affect development dependencies
# that are not included in production builds.

# =============================================================================
# Accepted Risks - Business Decision
# =============================================================================

# Note: Document any vulnerabilities that have been accepted as risks
# after security review. Include:
# - CVE ID
# - Affected package and version
# - Why it's accepted
# - Planned remediation date (if applicable)

# =============================================================================
# False Positives
# =============================================================================

# Note: Add vulnerabilities that are confirmed false positives.
# Explain why they don't apply to this project.

# =============================================================================
# Unfixable - Awaiting Upstream Patches
# =============================================================================

# Note: Vulnerabilities with no available fix yet.
# Monitor these and remove from ignore list when patches are available.

# =============================================================================
# Instructions for Adding Entries
# =============================================================================
#
# 1. Always add a comment explaining why the vulnerability is ignored
# 2. Include the date when the entry was added
# 3. Add a review date or condition for re-evaluation
# 4. Link to relevant issue or security review documentation
#
# Example:
# # CVE-2024-12345 - golang.org/x/crypto
# # Affects SSH parsing, not used in our application
# # Added: 2025-12-04
# # Review: When updating to Go 1.26
# CVE-2024-12345

# GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2 - github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/aws/protocol/eventstream
# Affects parsing malicious event stream messages, not applicable to our usage
# Added: 2026-04-18
# Review: When updating aws-sdk-go-v2
GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2

# CVE-2026-34040 - github.com/docker/docker
# Moby Authorization bypass vulnerability, development environment tool only
# Added: 2026-04-18
# Review: When updating docker in dependencies
CVE-2026-34040

# CVE-2026-33997 - github.com/docker/docker
# Moby Privilege validation bypass during plugin installation, development environment tool only
# Added: 2026-04-18
# Review: When updating docker in dependencies
CVE-2026-33997
